    "doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.18508676",
    "abstract": "This report summarises the findings of the Marine Spatial Planning Addressing Climate Effects project (MSPACE, 2021-2026) for the East Marine Plan area (England, UK). It includes key findings from novel research into: 1) the potential effects of climate change in this region of UK marine waters; 2) the structure of the region's blue economy; and 3) knowledge co-creation activities with marine stakeholders in the region. Through these activities, we draw up key recommendations for climate-resilient, economically sensible and socially acceptable strategies to manage marine space in the East Marine Plan area, leading to climate change adaptation and mitigation.",
    "field": "Climate-smart marine spatial planning",
    "problem": "This paper addresses the challenge of incorporating climate change into marine spatial planning by exploring alternative management scenarios to design effective, economically viable, and socially acceptable climate-smart plans for the UK's East Marine Plan area, a process complicated by a lack of established, integrated methods.",
    "method": "This paper proposes a method of co-creating and evaluating alternative climate-smart spatial management scenarios with stakeholders, using environmental and socio-economic analysis to identify acceptable strategies for climate adaptation and mitigation in marine planning.",
    "task": "The task is to develop and assess alternative climate-smart spatial management scenarios for the East Marine Plan area to provide recommendations for incorporating climate change adaptation and mitigation into marine planning.",
